#%PAM-1.0
# buchhwin-shell lock screen: a security key (a YubiKey or another FIDO2 key)
# through pam_u2f. Installed only by `scripts/security-key.py setup`
# (Settings > Lock Screen > Security key) and removed by its `off`, never by
# the installer. lock.qml runs this service first when lock.securityKey is
# "auto", and nothing else: a key that is not plugged in ends it at once and
# without a word, a wrong PIN or no touch end it too, and the lock goes on
# with buchhwin-lock (the fingerprint as lock.fingerprint says) or
# buchhwin-lock-password as before.
# pam_u2f asks for the key's PIN (pinverification=1) only once it has found a
# plugged key that holds one of the user's credentials
# (~/.config/Yubico/u2f_keys, read relative to the home directory whatever
# XDG_CONFIG_HOME says), then for a touch (cue). The origin is fixed rather
# than the host name, so a renamed machine keeps its keys. No password and no
# faillock here: the key counts its own wrong PINs.
auth     sufficient  pam_u2f.so cue pinverification=1 authfile=.config/Yubico/u2f_keys origin=pam://buchhwin-shell appid=pam://buchhwin-shell
auth     required    pam_deny.so
account  required    pam_permit.so
